# autotrade (quant.jsyoo.dev) — the crontab block for user ubuntu on the Oracle server.
# NOT installed. Installing it needs the owner's go (ops notes 안전), then:
#   crontab -l > ~/crontab.bak.$(date +\%F)        (keep the old table)
#   (crontab -l; cat deploy/autotrade.cron) | crontab -
# Remove: delete the block from `crontab -e`. Nothing else is installed by it.
#
# Times: the server's clock and cron run in UTC. This block has no time of day in it on
# purpose: cron wakes the tick every 5 minutes and `python -m autotrade.jobs tick` decides in KST
# (and in New York time for the US session, daylight saving included) what is due — the dividend
# download 08:00, the check 08:30, the retry 09:30, each stage at its own time (KR 09:05, FX 09:10,
# US open 22:30 or 23:30), the snapshot 16:00, then the backup — and how late each may still run
# (autotrade/jobs/schedule.py). Never translate those times into cron fields here.
#
# - flock -n: when the previous tick is still running the new one exits at once. The tick also
#   holds its own lock (data/autotrade.db-jobs.lock), which manual commands respect.
# - timeout 10m: a tick stuck on a network call is stopped; each step is one database
#   transaction, so the next tick picks up where it stopped.
# - Secrets: the tick reads one key, DART_API_KEY (Korean filings for the AI rule's daily watch),
#   from the file AUTOTRADE_SECRETS_ENV names; nothing else of that file is read
#   (autotrade/config.py read_env_key). Without it DART shows 'no-key' on the health screen and
#   the Korean filing watch stops. Without KRX_ID/KRX_PW pykrx cannot log in.
# - Live orders (phase 3, autotrade/PHASE3.md 2.1 and 4): AUTOTRADE_LIVE_ORDERS=1 on the tick's
#   line is the first of two keys, on since the owner's go (2026-10-13, after the old quant's
#   cron lines were removed: they shared the Toss client and each new token revoked the other's).
#   The second is the mode 'live' the owner sets on the mode screen with the PIN; until then the
#   tick only reads the account. With the key the tick reads TOSS_CLIENT_ID, TOSS_CLIENT_SECRET
#   and TOSS_ACCOUNT_NO from the same file (one key at a time, nothing else of it), keeps the
#   token in data/autotrade-toss/ (0700, git-ignored), looks at the account every 5 minutes and
#   records it for the web. Taking the key off this line stops every Toss call at the next tick;
#   the mode stays whatever it was.
# - One JSON line per task that ran goes to data/logs/autotrade-jobs.log (rotated daily with the
#   other data/logs/*.log by deploy/logrotate-dashboard). A tick with nothing due writes nothing.
# - The line has no % (crontab would cut it there; ops notes §8).
# - Only `python -m autotrade.jobs migrate` (deploy.sh) changes the schema. A job that finds the
#   database at another schema (between a deploy's `git pull` and its `migrate`, or before the
#   first `migrate`) writes one line {"result": "schema-mismatch", ...} and exits 3, doing nothing.
*/5 * * * * cd /home/ubuntu/portfolio-dashboard && AUTOTRADE_LIVE_ORDERS=1 AUTOTRADE_SECRETS_ENV=/home/ubuntu/dotclaude/secrets/.env flock -n data/autotrade.db-cron.lock timeout 10m .venv/bin/python -m autotrade.jobs tick >> data/logs/autotrade-jobs.log 2>&1
#
# The AI rule's questions (PHASE2.md §6): `python -m autotrade.jobs ai` takes the due AI tasks
# (filing extraction and screening, sell and buy confirmations, the monthly review, the quarterly
# discovery, switches) and asks the subscription CLI (`claude -p`, never the paid API).
# - Its own line and its own lock (data/autotrade.db-ai.lock, and flock -n here): a model call
#   has no time limit (ops notes §7), so there is no `timeout` and it never holds the tick.
# - AUTOTRADE_AI_CALLS=1 is the owner's go, given 2026-10-12 (installed that night after one
#   smoke call). Without it the runner calls nothing, records nothing, and the tasks wait: take
#   it off this line (and the server's crontab) to stop all model calls. Calls use the
#   subscription only, never the paid API.
# - The CLI: cron's PATH is /usr/bin:/bin, which has no `claude`. AUTOTRADE_CLAUDE_BIN names the
#   server's wrapper /usr/local/bin/claude (it puts the newest nvm node first on PATH and runs the
#   CLI). Without it the runner still looks there and in ~/.nvm (autotrade/ai/cli.py
#   find_claude); a CLI it cannot find is a source down on the health screen, never a failed task.
# - Secrets: like the tick, the runner reads DART_API_KEY from AUTOTRADE_SECRETS_ENV (it reads
#   Korean filing texts); without it Korean filing tasks wait and DART shows 'no-key'.
# - The CLI runs in the empty folder data/ai-cwd with a scrubbed environment: no ANTHROPIC_*,
#   no cloud or repository credentials, no AUTOTRADE_* (the secrets file's path stays here). It
#   uses the server user's own `claude` login under ~/.claude.
# - One JSON line per run with work goes to data/logs/autotrade-ai.log; the traceback of a task
#   that broke goes there too (stderr).
*/5 * * * * cd /home/ubuntu/portfolio-dashboard && AUTOTRADE_AI_CALLS=1 AUTOTRADE_CLAUDE_BIN=/usr/local/bin/claude AUTOTRADE_SECRETS_ENV=/home/ubuntu/dotclaude/secrets/.env flock -n data/autotrade.db-ai-cron.lock .venv/bin/python -m autotrade.jobs ai >> data/logs/autotrade-ai.log 2>&1
